<title>UK: Merrill Lynch says European research head quits.</title>
<headline>Merrill Lynch says European research head quits.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merrill Lynch International said on Monday that its head of European equity research Andre Sharon was leaving the company.</p>
<p>A Merrill spokesman said the investment bank was sorry to see Sharon go, describing him as &quot;well respected and well liked&quot; in the firm.</p>
<p>Market sources said Sharon was leaving to take up the position of director of European research at Dutch financial services giant ABN AMRO Hoare Govett, but Merrill could not confirm this and Sharon himself was not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- Alexander Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7719</p>
